{"user": "When White played a3 after my c8, the system said only one square was legal so g2 was played for me. I had other empty squares \u2014 does that mean g2 was literally my only legal trap, or is there a rule I missed about forced play?", "user_ts": "2026-08-15T00:23:38.071976+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 if the system showed only **g2** as marked legal, then **g2 was literally your only legal move**.\n\nRule reminder: an empty square is legal only if placing Black there would **flip at least one White disc** by bracketing a line of White discs between the new Black disc and another Black disc.\n\nSo having other empty squares doesn\u2019t matter unless they flip something.\n\nAlso: in Othello you **must move if you have any legal move**. You only **pass** when you have **zero** legal moves. If there\u2019s exactly one legal move, it\u2019s forced.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-15T00:23:38.071976+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-15T00:23:43.071976+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 2, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "Move Verdict": 1, "Local Justification": 2}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.6666666666666666, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Move Verdict": 0.3333333333333333, "Local Justification": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Positive Feedback",