{"user": "After my a8 move it only flipped b7. Why didn\u2019t it flip discs along the a-file too \u2014 is the whole a-file not considered a trapped line because it wasn\u2019t bounded on both ends by black?", "user_ts": "2026-08-15T00:23:53.071976+00:00", "assistant": "Exactly: the **a-file was not a trapped line** unless there was a Black disc at the far end.\n\nWhen you played **a8**, each direction is checked separately. Up the a-file would need:\n\n**a8 = new Black**, then one or more **White** discs, then a **Black** disc before the board edge.\n\nIf it was like:\n\n**a8 Black \u2013 a7 White \u2013 a6 White \u2013 \u2026 \u2013 a1 White \u2013 edge**\n\nthen nothing flips, because the edge of the board does **not** count as a Black disc.\n\nSo only the line through **b7** flipped because that direction was actually bounded by Black on both ends.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-15T00:23:53.071976+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-15T00:23:58.071976+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 2, "General Principle": 2, "Board Report": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 0.6666666666666666, "General Principle": 0.6666666666666666, "Board Report": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback"